This is just like that time I accidentally became a cop and solved crimes! Except this time I actually understood what was happening the WHOLE TIME!

Here's what I figured out (and I'm actually proud I understood this stuff):

1. **The Cart** - It's like a bag, but for NUMBERS and STUFF! I used a map so when you add the same thing twice, it just adds up the quantities instead of making duplicates. SMART!

2. **Remove Item** - If you try to remove more than you have, it just... deletes the whole thing. Like when I eat all the waffles and there are no more waffles.

3. **Discounts** - Only ONE discount at a time (the second one replaces the first - like how my new favorite song always replaces my old favorite song). Percent off calculates from the subtotal, fixed amount just subtracts. If the discount is bigger than the cart total, you get FREE STUFF! (Well, zero dollars.)

4. **Subtotal vs Total** - Subtotal is BEFORE discounts (the scary number), Total is AFTER discounts (the happy number).

